        "We negate and exponentiate these distances to ensure the lowest distance is represented as the highest number as a convention. \n",
        "\n",
        "Then, we divide by the total to standardize the distances between zero and 1. The nearest centroid will always have the highest affinity, so in this way we are using it to classify the formula.\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\delta_s(\\mathbf{x}) = \\lVert \\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{c}_s \\rVert\n",
        "$$ {#eq-distance}\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "a_s(\\mathbf{x}) = \\frac{\\exp\\big(-\\delta_s(\\mathbf{x})\\big)}{\\sum_{s' \\in \\mathcal{S}} \\exp\\big(-\\delta_{s'}(\\mathbf{x})\\big)}\n",
        "$$ {#eq-affinity}\n",
        "\n",
